sec.p:
The methodological quality assessments of the RCTs and non-RCTs are briefly showed in Table 1, and summarized in Supplementary Fig. 1 and Supplementary Table 1. Of the 5 RCTs, 3 were classified as low risk of bias and 2 as high risk. Based on the MINORS scoring system for non-RCTs, 12 points for 4 articles, and the scores of other 24 studies ranged from 13 to 22 points. Overall, the included studies were of moderate quality. The funnel plot constructed for publication bias evaluation showed a slight asymmetry (Fig. 2
). Nevertheless, the Egger’s regression analysis demonstrated that the visual asymmetry was not significant (95% CI of intercept −2.44 to 0.27; p = 0.11) (Fig. 3
).Fig. 2
Funnel plot for publication bias evaluation.Fig. 3
Egger’s regression analysis for publication bias.
